The space is recovered from Whisper's block text, not by inserting a space between any two Latin characters: that would split words like 'Easy' into 'E a s y', since every letter is its own unit. It is kept as a space_before flag rather than a leading space in the unit's word, because the phrase grouper maps tokenizer output back to units by character offsets in the joined text; a space inside a word would shift those offsets. The tokenizer still sees the text without spaces, which only affects phrase boundaries, not the text. Spaces next to Japanese or Chinese characters (日本語 3 回) are dropped as before, since written Japanese and Chinese don't use them.
